The diagonal approximable map into a product of a system with itself.

<!-- formalization -->

**Definition (`diag`).** The diagonal map of a neighbourhood system is the pairing of the identity with itself.

*Proof.* By definition. ∎

**Theorem (`diag_rel`).** The diagonal relates a neighbourhood to a product neighbourhood precisely when both projections of that product neighbourhood relate under the identity.

*Proof.* Unpack the pairing relation. ∎

**Theorem (`toElementMap_diag`).** Elementwise, the diagonal sends each ideal element to its self-pair.

*Proof.* Apply the pairing and identity evaluations. ∎

**Theorem (`proj₀_comp_diag`).** The first projection after the diagonal recovers the identity.

*Proof.* Invoke the corresponding law for pairing with identities. ∎
